{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q5204319","formula":"C₁₆H₁₇N₃S","hill":"C16H17N3S","elements":["H","C","N","S"],"composition":{"C":16.0,"H":17.0,"N":3.0,"S":1.0},"names":{"en":"DASB"},"descriptions":{"en":"DASB, also known as 3-amino-4-(2-dimethylaminomethylphenylsulfanyl)-benzonitrile, is a compound that binds to the serotonin transporter. Labeled with carbon-11 — a radioactive isotope — it has been used as a radioligand in neuroimaging with positron emission tomography (PET) since around year 2000. In this context it is regarded as one of the superior radioligands for PET study of the serotonin transporter in the brain, since it has high selectivity for the serotonin transporter."},"fame":3,"pubchemCid":10446567,"mass":283.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CN(C)CC1=CC=CC=C1SC2=C(C=C(C=C2)C#N)N","inchikey":"UVWLEPXXYOYDGR-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"3-amino-4-[2-[(dimethylamino)methyl]phenyl]sulfanylbenzonitrile","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"10446567","atoms":37,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.405,"y":0.949,"z":-1.295,"el":"S"},{"x":-4.315,"y":1.095,"z":0.601,"el":"N"},{"x":2.235,"y":0.454,"z":-2.84,"el":"N"},{"x":6.065,"y":-0.138,"z":1.597,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.854,"y":1.063,"z":0.663,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.307,"y":-0.296,"z":0.317,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.226,"y":-0.45,"z":-0.541,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.925,"y":-1.404,"z":0.887,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.753,"y":-1.73,"z":-0.834,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.777,"y":0.759,"z":-0.745,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.815,"y":2.41,"z":1.0,"el":"C"},{"x":1.21,"y":0.677,"z":-0.623,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.452,"y":-2.683,"z":0.595,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.367,"y":-2.846,"z":-0.266,"el":"C"},{"x":2.341,"y":0.462,"z":-1.43,"el":"C"},{"x":1.37,"y":0.675,"z":0.772,"el":"C"},{"x":3.595,"y":0.252,"z":-0.857,"el":"C"},{"x":2.624,"y":0.464,"z":1.346,"el":"C"},{"x":3.736,"y":0.253,"z":0.531,"el